though 2018 Halloween recaptures the  stripped-down aesthetics of carpenters  original vision there's still a handful  of treats scattered among its tricks  waiting to be found by sharp eyed fans  come along with us as we give you a  brief rundown of the secrets hiding in  Halloween shadows just watch out for the  boogeyman and spoilers understandably  the focus of much of Halloween type has  been on Jamie Lee Curtis and the return  of the role that made her famous Laurie  Strode curtis's 1978 performance remains  iconic in the annals of horror history  earning her the lingering title of  scream queen she played Laurie again  across three other decades starring in  1981 s Halloween to 1998 Halloween h2o  and 2002 s Halloween resurrection  she even lent her voice to Halloween 3  season of the witch the unrelated  standalone entry in which she can be  heard as an announcer however while  those previous sequels tended to leave  Laurie sidelined in a hospital bed or  killed off after a glorified cameo the  2018 film is fully dedicated to her  story exploring the trauma that has  affected her life and her family  less obvious are some other returning  performers joining Curtis Michael Myers  is played by two different actors in  carpenters film  Nick Castle was the man behind the mask  while tony moran portrayed the killer  for the single scene in which his face  can be glimpsed castle is back this time  around sharing the role of Michael with  newcomer James Jude Courtney the new  Halloween takes us back to the fictional  town of Haddonfield Illinois the small  community once rocked by Michael Myers  as original murders while the story  keeps a tight focus on Laurie her  daughter Karen and her granddaughter  Allison the filmmakers nonetheless made  sure to include a few nods to the  continuing history of the town around  them the original Halloween was shot  during the summer in California  grappling with a very modest budget  carpenter's crew had to simulate a  Midwestern autumn by spreading dead  leaves on the ground  despite the trees visibly blooming in  several shots the new movie shot in  South Carolina in the winter recreates  this unsettling juxtaposition during an  early scene in which Alison and her  friends stroll down Hatton fields leaf  strewn sidewalks under green foliage  beyond the visuals citizens are  name-checked to with Alison's boyfriend  Cameron Elam established as the son of  Lonnie Elam a troublemaking classmate of  young Tommy Doyle  in 1978 in addition to set dressing and  name drops Stephen Gordon green and  Danny McBride peppered their new  Halloween with a number of cinematic  allusions to its predecessor from in  jokes and references to inversions and  reversals it will be impossible for  longtime Halloween fans to watch this  new take without feeling a certain sense  of deja vu this is obvious right from  the opening titles which revived the  jack-o'-lantern that kicked off the  first movie Michaels 2018 hospital  Escape mirror says first with white gown  mental patients wandering eerily by the  glow of car headlights later a familiar  playground rhyme echoes during the  trick-or-treat sequence the real fun  begins though when laurie herself takes  the place of michael in a number of  familiar moments particularly the  climactic balcony fall and subsequent  disappearance her face also looms in the  darkness behind him at one point just as  he had loomed behind her in the end the  fire that at last consumes the shape  also burns a dollhouse which bears a  passing resemblance to the original  Myers home while the new movie ignores  all the sequels that preceded it McBride  and Greene still set out with an  intention to pay tribute to every  Halloween movie their film states that  Michael has been in custody  ever since that fateful night in 1978  making it clear that none of his later  shenanigans ever happened in its world  however winks and nods abound to consult  fans who might be miffed about this new  timeline 1981 s Halloween 2 revealed  that Laurie and Michael were siblings  suggesting that his killing spree was  somehow motivated by his own bloodline  further sequels took this concept  further sending the shape after more  relatives and proposing an ancient curse  as his motivation the new movie has  Allison quickly dispelled the notion of  Laurie and Michael being sister and  brother wasn't it her brother converted  all those babies interesting yeah it was  not her brother that's the main and  people made up more subtle sequel  references include a glimpse at  Halloween three sinister masks a gas  station bearing a strong resemblance to  a set from the return of Michael Myers  and a public restroom setting similar to  a scene in h2o  Donald Pleasance was one of the few  consistent mainstays of the Halloween  sequels playing dr. Sam Loomis and five  films before his death acting as  something of a van Helsing to Michael's  Dracula Loomis dedicated his entire life  to stopping his famous patient even when  no  believed him about the danger they were  in in the first movie he sums up the  sheep's unknowable motivations as  succinctly as possible I realized that  what was living behind that boy's eyes  was purely and simply evil the new movie  pays rather subtle but brilliant homage  to this idea though the 2018 Halloween  takes place in a timeline where Michael  never escaped again during the late  Loomis's lifetime  his dedication still plays a major role  and the character even makes a cassette  tape cameo via a pleasant sound alight  we are introduced to a man dubbed the  new Loomis by lorry doctor Sartain whose  unhealthy obsession with understanding  Michael's motivations leads him to  betray the heroes towards the film's  climax in the end the bad doctor learns  that what Laurie and Loomis have always  said is true there's no reasoning with  pure evil as a matter of fact it was
 

